# Testing the NR Markdown workbook

## Cell types

We can have three different kinds of cells

* Markdown (the default)
* NRQL
* Lua

Code cells (NRQL and Lua) are fended with standard markdown code blocks. ie: Three backticks and then `nrql` or `lua`

Can this contain variables?
{{ results.top_app.rows[1].facet }}

```nrql
/***
  title: Busiest app, last week
  var: top_app
  chart: billboard
***/
FROM Transaction
SELECT count(*)
FACET appName
SINCE 1 week ago
LIMIT 4
```

```nrql
/***
  title: Metrics for the busiest app
  chart: line
  attributes: stacked smoothed
***/
FROM Metric SELECT count(*) WHERE appName = '{{ results.top_app.rows[1].facet }}' SINCE 1 week ago TIMESERIES 1 day
```

```nrql
/***
title: Transactions for the busiest app
var: transactions
chart: none
***/

FROM Transaction SELECT count(*) AS count WHERE appName = '{{ results.top_app.rows[1].facet }}' SINCE 1 week ago
```

```nrql
/***
title: Errors for the busiest app
var: errors
chart: none
***/

FROM TransactionError SELECT count(*) AS count WHERE appName = '{{ results.top_app.rows[1].facet }}' SINCE 1 week ago
```

## Running lua scripts

In this exmaple, two previous results (which have hidden graphs, but still run and save results) are referenced to build a result from the independent data sets.

The `emit` function is used to push data into the chartting system.

```lua
--[[
title: Transactions vs. errors
chart: bar
]]

emit({
  rows = {
    { facet = "Transaction", count = results.transactions.rows[1].count },
    { facet = "TransactionError", count = results.errors.rows[1].count },
  },
})
```

```graphql

# title: Entity Search
# var: entity_search
query FindEntity($account_id: Int!, $query: String) {
  actor {
    account(id: $account_id)
    entitySearch(query: $query) {
      results { entities {
        guid 
        account { name id }
        name
        reporting
        tags { key values }
      }}
    }
  }
}
```
```variables
{
  "account_id": {{ config.account_id }},
  "query": "name = '{{ results.top_app.rows[1].facet }}'"
}
```

```lua
--[[
title: Entity tag count
chart: billboard
]]

local entities = results.entity_search.data.actor.entitySearch.results.entities
local entity = assert(entities[1], "No matching entity found")

emit({
  rows = {
    { ["Tag Count"] = #entity.tags }
  }
})
```
